Authors and Contributors
========================

Jim Peters <jim@uazu.net>
  Original author of fidlib, fiview, and firun (2002–2004).
  Brighton, UK. http://uazu.net/

JamesHight
  Community patches to fidlib: const-correctness, C++ guards, v0.9.11.
  https://github.com/JamesHight/fidlib

Jörg Simbrig <Josbrig@simbrig.de>
  Extensions to fidlib: SIMD/NEON acceleration, Overlap-Save FFT engine,
  Vulkan Compute and OpenCL backends, cmake modernisation (2025–2026).
  New components: fidgen (universal filter code generator, 8 output languages),
  fiview2 (Dear ImGui GUI workbench), fiview2 WebAssembly browser port,
  imtile (cockpit layout library), install scripts, manuals.

Acknowledgements
----------------

Dr. Tony Fisher (1956–2000), University of York, UK
  Author of mkfilter. The filter design algorithms in fidlib are based
  on techniques from his work, with permission from the University of York.
  http://www-users.cs.york.ac.uk/~fisher/mkfilter/

Robert Bristow-Johnson
  Author of the Audio EQ Cookbook, whose biquad filter formulas
  are implemented in fidlib's BpBq/LpBq/etc. filter family.
